  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 8 messages, including 1 that arrived while I worked, were decided and closed, and each patient got a reply.\n\nResults that arrived mid-work and changed two decisions (§7):\n- **Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: refill cancelled, review task created.** At first I renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill. The August potassium of 5.9 from St. Brigid was on a hemolyzed sample, so I used the last valid potassium (4.5, Jan 2026) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then a St. Brigid BMP from 10/20 arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001) before it was dispensed and sent you a review task (task-t0022). The repeat BMP is still ordered. I sent him a corrected message and wrote a chart note.\n- **Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg: refill cancelled, review task created.** At first I renewed it because the 10/06 creatinine had risen only 24% after the 9/18 dose increase. The lab then corrected that creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49, a 35% rise, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0005) before it was dispensed and sent you a review task (task-t0023). I sent him a corrected message and wrote a chart note.\n- **Both patients now have no active lisinopril order.** Placing each renewal had automatically stopped the old order (mr-00283 and mr-00295), so both await your decision. Mr. Odum is out of refills and Mr. Price says his supply is finished.\n\nOther decisions:\n- **Samuel Price, metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0006).** His message and both pharmacy requests were treated as one request. His eGFR is 58 (corrected from 65), and an outside HbA1c of 7.1% from 8/19 counts as within 6 months.\n- **Marcus Webb (pt-0031), lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply with no refills (mr-t0011), and a BMP is ordered (sr-t0013).** His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago, but he had a visit on 9/28/2026. A potassium of 4.6 measured on its own arrived during the work; it does not count as a BMP, so the decision stands.\n- **Marcus Webb, metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0012).** His eGFR is 92 and HbA1c 6.9% (both 9/28). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (wrong patient's sample).\n- **Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070), lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled, review task created (task-t0017).** On the 10/19 BMP his creatinine was 1.46, 46% above the 1.00 drawn before the 9/28 dose increase. His current order (mr-70002) is still active, not held. He also had an urgent care visit on 9/28 for gastroenteritis with dehydration.\n\nStill open for you:\n- The 3 review tasks above.\n- 3 new items in your results queue (for Odum, Price and Webb). I reviewed and acted on them but left them open for you to sign off.\n- 9 older results-queue items for other patients, including critical potassium results for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4). I did not touch these because they were outside the messages queue.",
